     The rraanndd() function computes a sequence of pseudo-random integers in the
     range of 0 to RAND_MAX, inclusive.

     The ssrraanndd() function seeds the algorithm with the _s_e_e_d parameter.  Re‐
     peatable sequences of rraanndd() output may be obtained by calling ssrraanndd()
     with the same _s_e_e_d.  rraanndd() is implicitly initialized as if ssrraanndd(_1) had
     been invoked explicitly.

     In FreeBSD 13, rraanndd() is implemented using the same 128-byte state LFSR
     generator algorithm as random(3).  However, the legacy rraanndd__rr() function
     is not (and can not be, because of its limited _*_c_t_x size).  rraanndd__rr() im‐
     plements the historical, poor-quality Park-Miller 32-bit LCG and should
     not be used in new designs.

IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     Since FreeBSD 13, rraanndd() is implemented with the same generator as
     random(3), so the low-order bits should no longer be significantly worse
     than the high-order bits.

